---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageIntro from '../../components/PageIntro.astro';
import PageCTA from '../../components/PageCTA.astro';
import Icon from '../../components/Icon.astro';
import { site } from '../../data/site';
---
<BaseLayout title="About Dr Sarah Cook" description="Meet the Clinical Psychologist behind Curious Brain and discover the thinking behind the printable resources." wide>
  <PageIntro eyebrow="About Sarah & Curious Brain" title="The psychologist behind The Curious Brain Toolkit" />
  <section class="section"><div class="container story-grid">
    <div class="creator-profile"><img src="/images/curious-brain-mascot.webp" alt="The Curious Brain mascot, a friendly brain with a magnifying glass" width="280" height="272" /><p class="eyebrow">The mind behind the toolkit</p><h2>{site.creator.name}</h2><p>{site.creator.role}<br />Creator of The Curious Brain Toolkit</p><span class="profile-rule" aria-hidden="true"></span><p class="profile-caption">Psychology-informed.<br />Curiosity-led.</p></div>
    <div class="story-copy">
      <p>I’m Dr Sarah Cook, an HCPC-registered Clinical Psychologist with a Doctorate in Clinical Psychology and many years’ experience supporting children, young people, families and schools.</p>
      <p>In my clinical work, I often noticed that children were offered coping strategies before they had been given enough help to understand what was happening for them. I created The Curious Brain Toolkit to offer a different starting point: slowing down, noticing what is happening, developing shared understanding and then exploring what might help.</p>
      <p>The resources translate psychological ideas into clear, practical tools for shared conversations. They are psychology-informed and neurodiversity-affirming, while leaving room for each child’s own words, interests and pace.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href="/our-approach/">How the approach works <Icon name="arrow" /></a>
    </div>
  </div></section>
  <section class="values-section"><div class="container"><div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">What guides the toolkit</p><h2>Small steps. Shared understanding.</h2></div><div class="info-grid">
    <article class="info-card"><Icon name="eye" /><h3>Notice before solving</h3><p>Start with what the child is experiencing. Understanding can come before deciding what to change.</p></article>
    <article class="info-card"><Icon name="people" /><h3>Explore together</h3><p>Use the resources alongside a child, making room for conversation and their own perspective.</p></article>
    <article class="info-card"><Icon name="leaf" /><h3>Keep it manageable</h3><p>Choose a relevant starting point, try a small next step and adjust as you learn together.</p></article>
  </div></div></section>
  <PageCTA />
</BaseLayout>
